---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/tag-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Tag study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of metadata tags for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="tag-study">
    <div class="shell tag-study-intro">
      <a class="tag-study-back" href="/prototypes/filter-study/">← Filter study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should small facts sit?</h1>
      <p class="tag-study-lede">Three treatments for the town and category labels that sit above a transformation title.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell tag-study-grid">
      <article class="tag-option"><p class="tag-option-name"><span>A</span> Boxed label</p><div class="tag-demo"><span class="study-tag study-tag--boxed">Dundrum</span><span class="study-tag study-tag--muted">Food &amp; drink</span></div><p>Clear and structured, with a small blue outline for the primary fact.</p></article>
      <article class="tag-option"><p class="tag-option-name"><span>B</span> Colour rule</p><div class="tag-demo"><span class="study-tag study-tag--rule">Dundrum</span><span class="study-tag study-tag--rule-muted">Food &amp; drink</span></div><p>Uses the selected link language: plain text, with colour and a small rule doing the work.</p></article>
      <article class="tag-option"><p class="tag-option-name"><span>C</span> Plain metadata</p><div class="tag-demo"><span class="study-tag study-tag--plain">Dundrum</span><span class="study-tag study-tag--plain-muted">Food &amp; drink</span></div><p>Most restrained. The two facts are separated by a dot and no longer feel like controls.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
